'''''The Lima News''''' is a local daily newspaper aimed at residents in [[Allen County, Ohio|Allen]], [[Auglaize County, Ohio|Auglaize]], [[Hancock County, Ohio|Hancock]], [[Hardin County, Ohio|Hardin]], [[Logan County, Ohio|Logan]], [[Mercer County, Ohio|Mercer]], [[Putnam County, Ohio|Putnam]], [[Shelby County, Ohio|Shelby]] and [[Van Wert County, Ohio|Van Wert]] counties in [[Ohio]], USA. Its headquarters is located in [[Lima, Ohio]].

== History ==
The newspaper was first printed on July 21, 1926.<ref>{{Cite news|last=Ellerbrock|first=Josh|date=February 22, 2020|title=The Lima News stands on century-old yet strong foundation|url=https://www.limaohio.com/news/398791/the-lima-news-stands-on-century-old-yet-strong-foundation|access-date=Jul 25, 2020|website=The Lima News}}</ref> The paper was owned by [[Freedom Communications]], a privately held California-based company whose flagship paper is the ''[[Orange County Register]]'', until 2012, when it was sold to Ohio Community Media, an affiliate of the private equity firm Versa Capital Management.<ref>{{cite news|last=Milbourn |first=Mary Ann|url=http://www.ocregister.com/articles/versa-354643-sale-group.html |title=Freedom Communications sells 4 Midwest papers |work=Orange County Register |access-date=November 19, 2022}}<br>- {{cite news |url=http://newsdemocrat.com/main.asp?SectionID=1&SubSectionID=1&ArticleID=135718&TM=28723.68 |title=OCM purchases the Lima News |work=News Democrat|access-date=2012-08-25 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120604234806/http://newsdemocrat.com/main.asp?SectionID=1 |archive-date=2012-06-04 }}</ref> Under Freedom Communications' ownership, ''The Lima News'' took a libertarian editorial position on issues.

In 2012, Versa merged Ohio Community Media, the Freedom papers it had acquired, [[Impressions Media]] and [[Heartland Publications]] into a new company, [[Civitas Media]].<ref>{{cite news |access-date=April 10, 2017|url= http://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20120911006840/en/Versa-Capital-Announces-Formation-Civitas-Media-LLC |work=Business Wire | title= Versa Capital Announces the Formation of Civitas Media, LLC }}</ref> Civitas Media sold its Ohio papers to AIM Media Midwest in 2017.<ref>{{Cite web| title = Quarterly Updates - 2nd Quarter 2017| publisher = Dirks, Van Essen & Murray| access-date = 2017-10-28| date = 2017-06-30| url = http://dirksvanessen.com/articles/view/225/2nd-quarter-2017/}}</ref>

